text.section:
A business trust shall keep a copy of the following records:

Its articles or restated articles of trust and all amendments to them currently in effect;


Its governing instrument and all amendments to it currently in effect;


Resolutions adopted by its trustees creating one or more classes or series of beneficial interests, and fixing their relative rights, preferences, and limitations, if beneficial interests issued pursuant to those resolutions are outstanding;


The minutes of all meetings of beneficial owners, and records of all action taken by beneficial owners without a meeting, for the past three years;


All written communications to beneficial owners generally within the past three years; and


A list of the names and business addresses of its current trustees and officers.
